---
// Case G — Transit Access & Urban Equity. Spec: docs/spec-transit-equity.html (G5).
// Signature moment: "the hour" — the 60-minute reachable area blooming outward from a
// kelurahan along the network, on a 2-D canvas (works with WebGL off, which is the
// designed-for case). Chapters argue the equity read; the methodology carries the gates.
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css";
---

<html lang="en" data-case="transit" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>The Hour · Transit Access &amp; Urban Equity in Jabodetabek</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Who can reach work and a hospital within an hour on public transport in Greater Jakarta — and who cannot. TransJakarta, KRL, MRT and LRT on one routing graph." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700;800&family=Public+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <!-- ───────────────────────── HERO ───────────────────────── -->
    <header class="hero" id="hero">
      <div class="hero-canvas" id="hero-map">
        <canvas id="hero-c"></canvas>
        <div class="hero-scrim"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">Demo Lab · Jabodetabek</span>
        <h1>The hour.</h1>
        <p class="lede">An hour on public transport buys a Menteng resident about a tenth of
        Greater Jakarta's job-dense floorspace. Sixty minutes from a desa in Kabupaten Bogor
        buys a walk. This is that hour, computed door-to-door over every footpath, busway,
        commuter rail, MRT and LRT in the region — and the hour itself is a choice, so the
        half-hour and the three-quarter-hour are published beside it.</p>
        <div class="hero-hud" id="hero-hud" hidden>
          <div class="hud-main">
            <span class="hud-num" id="hud-clock">00:00</span>
            <span class="hud-lab">minutes from <b id="hud-origin">—</b></span>
          </div>
          <div class="hud-stats">
            <span><b id="hud-jobs">—</b> of the region's job-dense floorspace</span>
            <span><b id="hud-hosp">—</b> hospitals · <b id="hud-pop">—</b> of its people</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hud-actions">
            <button class="btn" id="hero-replay" type="button">Replay the hour</button>
            <button class="btn ghost" id="hero-shuffle" type="button">Another origin</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="stamp" id="hero-stamp">Scheduled times · weekday 07:00–09:00 departures · p50</span>
      </div>
      <a class="scroll-cue" href="#ch1" aria-label="Scroll to the first chapter"><span></span></a>
    </header>

    <main>
      <!-- ─────────────────── CH 1 · the network ─────────────────── -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch1">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="ch-num">01</span>
          <div>
            <h2>One network, four systems</h2>
            <p class="ch-lede">A busway that carries a million rides a day, 98 Mikrotrans
            capillaries feeding it, five commuter-rail lines, one MRT and two LRTs — assembled
            here into a single routing graph with every OSM footpath in the metro.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-wrap reveal">
          <div class="net-map" id="net-map"><canvas id="net-c"></canvas>
            <div class="map-note" id="net-note">2-D CANVAS · OSM ODbL</div>
          </div>
          <aside class="net-side">
            <div class="legend" id="net-legend"></div>
            <div class="stat-grid" id="net-stats"></div>
            <p class="caveat"><b>Rail is hand-encoded.</b> No operator publishes a GTFS feed for
            KRL, MRT or either LRT. Their timetables here are built from the operators' own
            published headways and end-to-end journey times, distributed along OSM geometry —
            so every rail time carries a ±15 % caveat. The bus layers are the official
            TransJakarta feed.</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <p class="sowhat reveal">So what: the network looks continuous on a map. Access is not
        the network — it is what the network reaches inside a working hour, and that is a much
        smaller thing.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- ─────────────────── CH 2 · an hour from home ─────────────────── -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch2">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="ch-num">02</span>
          <div>
            <h2>An hour from home</h2>
            <p class="ch-lede">Every one of Jabodetabek's kelurahan and desa, shaded by the share
            of the region's job-dense floorspace it can reach on public transport within the
            cutoff. Click any unit for its own isochrone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="controls reveal">
          <div class="ctl">
            <label for="cutoff">Cutoff</label>
            <div class="seg" id="cutoff" role="group" aria-label="Travel time cutoff"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="ctl">
            <label for="scenario">Network</label>
            <div class="seg" id="scenario" role="group" aria-label="Network scenario"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="ctl grow">
            <label for="search">Find a kelurahan</label>
            <input id="search" type="search" list="kel-list" placeholder="e.g. Menteng, Cikarang, Serpong" autocomplete="off" />
            <datalist id="kel-list"></datalist>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="map-wrap reveal">
          <div class="map" id="map"></div>
          <div class="tip" id="tip" hidden></div>
          <div class="ramp" id="ramp"></div>
          <aside class="panel" id="panel" hidden>
            <button class="panel-x" id="panel-close" type="button" aria-label="Close">×</button>
            <span class="panel-eyebrow" id="p-region">—</span>
            <h3 id="p-name">—</h3>
            <div class="panel-stats" id="p-stats"></div>
            <div class="panel-bars" id="p-bars"></div>
            <p class="panel-note" id="p-note"></p>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <div class="callouts reveal" id="callouts"></div>
        <p class="sowhat reveal" id="ch2-sowhat"></p>
      </section>

      <!-- ─────────────────── CH 3 · who is left out ─────────────────── -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch3">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="ch-num">03</span>
          <div>
            <h2>Who is left out</h2>
            <p class="ch-lede">Rank every resident by the access their kelurahan has, poorest
            access first, and plot the cumulative share of reachable opportunity against the
            cumulative share of people. A fair network would trace the diagonal.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="equity-wrap">
          <div class="lorenz reveal" id="lorenz"></div>
          <div class="equity-side reveal">
            <div class="bigstat"><span class="bignum" id="gini">—</span><span class="biglab">Gini of population-weighted 60-minute access</span></div>
            <div class="bigstat"><span class="bignum" id="palma">—</span><span class="biglab">Palma ratio — the top tenth's access over the bottom four tenths'</span></div>
            <div class="bigstat"><span class="bignum" id="nohosp">—</span><span class="biglab">of Jabodetabek's people cannot reach a single hospital in an hour <b>on scheduled public transport</b> — most of the region travels by motorcycle, which this does not model</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cutstrip reveal" id="cutstrip"></div>
        <p class="cutnote reveal">Every inequality number on this page is a property of the hour
        as much as of the network: a cumulative-opportunity measure counts what falls inside an
        arbitrary boundary, so the boundary has to be published with it.</p>
        <div class="tables reveal">
          <div class="tbl"><h4>Best served</h4><div id="tbl-best"></div></div>
          <div class="tbl"><h4>Worst served (population over 5,000)</h4><div id="tbl-worst"></div></div>
        </div>
        <p class="sowhat reveal" id="ch3-sowhat"></p>
      </section>

      <!-- ─────────────────── CH 4 · what each layer buys ─────────────────── -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch4">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="ch-num">04</span>
          <div>
            <h2>What each layer buys</h2>
            <p class="ch-lede">Rerun the same hour with the rail layer removed, then with no
            public transport at all. The gap between the three is what each system is worth to
            the median resident — and what it does to the distribution.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="layers reveal" id="layers"></div>
        <p class="sowhat reveal" id="ch4-sowhat"></p>
      </section>

      <!-- ─────────────────── METHOD ─────────────────── -->
      <section class="chapter method" id="method">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="ch-num">05</span>
          <div>
            <h2>How this was built, and where it is weak</h2>
            <p class="ch-lede">Scheduled times, not congestion. Frequency-aware routing over a
            two-hour morning peak. A floorspace proxy standing in for jobs. Every one of those
            choices is stated here, with the gates that tested them.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="method-grid">
          <div class="reveal"><h4>Validation gates</h4><div id="gates"></div></div>
          <div class="reveal"><h4>Hand-encoded rail timetables</h4><div id="rail-table"></div></div>
          <div class="reveal"><h4>Sources &amp; licences</h4><div id="sources"></div></div>
          <div class="reveal"><h4>Known limits</h4>
            <ul class="limits">
              <li><b>Jobs are a proxy.</b> The measure is non-residential built-up floorspace
              (GHS-BUILT-S NRES, 2020) — where workplaces are, not how many people work in them.
              It is called "job-dense floorspace" throughout and never "jobs".</li>
              <li><b>Scheduled, not congested.</b> R5 routes the published timetable. Real
              TransJakarta buses sit in traffic; real KRL trains hold at Manggarai.</li>
              <li><b>Angkot are largely missing.</b> Outside the TransJakarta feed and one
              community Bogor angkot feed, the paratransit that actually moves the periphery
              has no open timetable anywhere. Access in the outer kabupaten is therefore a
              floor, not an estimate.</li>
              <li><b>Rail timetables are hand-encoded</b> from published headways (±15 %).</li>
              <li><b>Walking access to transit is capped at 30 minutes</b>, the standard
              assumption; ojek and feeder angkot are not modelled.</li>
            </ul>
            <ul class="limits" id="limits-review"></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter review-cta" id="review">
        <span class="eyebrow">06 · Review</span>
        <h2>We had this instrument reviewed, adversarially.</h2>
        <p>An independent read of the same data against the published literature. It shows that
        the inequality headline is largely a property of the sixty-minute cut-off rather than of
        the network; that the whole system is relatively regressive on this measure, with 94 % of
        what it adds accruing to the 30 % of the region inside DKI; that the one check this build
        passed compares two different estimators; and it computes the poverty axis this page had
        been carrying as pending.</p>
        <a class="cta big" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/article`}>Read the review article →</a>
      </section>

      <section class="cta" id="cta">
        <h3>What this becomes for a client</h3>
        <p>The same graph answers the questions a planning agency, an employer or a developer
        actually asks: what a new corridor would add, which kelurahan a fare reform would reach,
        where a campus should sit so its workforce can get there. Congestion-adjusted times,
        fare and affordability layers, park-and-ride and future-network scenarios are the
        obvious next build.</p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="foot">
      <span class="stamp dim" id="foot-stamp">A DEMO-LAB CASE · STATIC SNAPSHOT</span>
      <span class="stamp dim">TransJakarta GTFS (licence unstated — attributed, written confirmation pending) · OpenStreetMap contributors ODbL · GHSL R2023A CC BY 4.0 · HDX healthsites ODbL · HDX COD-AB (BPS) CC BY-IGO · routing by r5py / R5</span>
    </footer>

    <script>
      import maplibregl from "maplibre-gl";
      import * as d3 from "d3";

      /* visible failure beats silent emptiness */
      const failBanner = (msg) => {
        let b = document.getElementById("err-banner");
        if (!b) {
          b = document.createElement("div"); b.id = "err-banner";
          b.style.cssText = "position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:99;background:#3A1E1A;color:#F2846B;font:12px ui-monospace,monospace;padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid #F2846B;";
          document.body.appendChild(b);
        }
        b.textContent = "⚠ " + msg;
      };
      addEventListener("error", (e) => failBanner("Script error: " + (e.message ?? e.type)));
      addEventListener("unhandledrejection", (e) => failBanner("Load error: " + (e.reason?.message ?? e.reason)));
      const sect = (name, fn) => { try { return fn(); } catch (err) { console.error(name, err); failBanner(`${name} failed: ${err.message ?? err}`); return null; } };

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const reduced = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
      const MODE_COLOR = { brt: "#E4562E", mikrotrans: "#8C6A5D", krl: "#3E8EDE", mrt: "#57B26A", lrt: "#E0A63F" };
      const MODE_LABEL = { brt: "TransJakarta BRT corridors", mikrotrans: "Mikrotrans (JAK) microbus", krl: "KRL Commuter Line", mrt: "MRT Jakarta", lrt: "LRT (Jabodebek · Jakarta)" };
      const RAMP = ["#15181F", "#3A2118", "#7E3418", "#C24A20", "#E4562E", "#F79C6A"];
      const ramp = d3.piecewise(d3.interpolateRgb, RAMP);
      const BAND = ["#F79C6A", "#E4562E", "#C24A20", "#8E3A1B", "#5C2814"]; // 0-15, -30, -45, -60, beyond
      const fx = (v, d = 3) => (typeof v === "number" && isFinite(v) ? v.toFixed(d) : "—");
      const pct = (v, d = 1) => (v === null || v === undefined || !isFinite(v) ? "—" : `${(v * 100).toFixed(d)}%`);
      const num = (v) => (v === null || v === undefined || !isFinite(v) ? "—" : d3.format(",")(Math.round(v)));
      const bandOf = (t) => (t <= 15 ? 0 : t <= 30 ? 1 : t <= 45 ? 2 : 3);

      const [geo, access, cells, net, equity, stats, hero, review] = await Promise.all([
        fetch(`${base}/data/adm4.geojson`).then((r) => r.json()),
        fetch(`${base}/data/access.json`).then((r) => r.json()),
        fetch(`${base}/data/cells.json`).then((r) => r.json()),
        fetch(`${base}/data/network.json`).then((r) => r.json()),
        fetch(`${base}/data/equity.json`).then((r) => r.json()),
        fetch(`${base}/data/stats.json`).then((r) => r.json()).catch(() => null),
        fetch(`${base}/data/hero.json`).then((r) => r.json()).catch(() => null),
        fetch(`${base}/data/review_summary.json`).then((r) => r.json()).catch(() => null),
      ]);

      const state = { cutoff: 60, scenario: "all", sel: null };
      const rows = access.rows;
      /* Frame the mainland. Kepulauan Seribu lies ~60 km offshore; including it in the bounds
         shrank Jabodetabek to a third of the frame. The islands stay in every number and in
         the tables — they are simply off-frame on the maps, which is stated in the note. */
      const B = (() => {
        let w = 180, s = 90, e = -180, n = -90;
        for (const f of geo.features) {
          if (/seribu/i.test(f.properties.r ?? "")) continue;
          const polys = f.geometry.type === "Polygon" ? [f.geometry.coordinates] : f.geometry.coordinates;
          for (const poly of polys) for (const ring of poly) for (const [x, y] of ring) {
            if (x < w) w = x; if (x > e) e = x; if (y < s) s = y; if (y > n) n = y;
          }
        }
        const padLon = (e - w) * 0.015, padLat = (n - s) * 0.015;
        return { w: w - padLon, s: s - padLat, e: e + padLon, n: n + padLat };
      })();

      const val = (id, sc = state.scenario, cut = state.cutoff) => {
        const r = rows[id]; if (!r || !r[sc]) return null;
        const a = r[sc][String(cut)]; return a ? a[0] : null;
      };
      /* Access is extremely concentrated, so the choropleth uses a square-root scale — stated
         on the legend — or nine tenths of the region would read as a single flat black. */
      const shadeT = (v) => Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (v ?? 0) / maxVal)));
      const maxVal = (() => {
        let m = 0; for (const id in rows) { const v = val(id, "all", 60); if (v > m) m = v; } return m || 1;
      })();

      /* ═════════ a reusable 2-D canvas map (the product, not a fallback) ═════════ */
      function canvasMap(canvas, opts = {}) {
        const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
        const hitCtx = document.createElement("canvas").getContext("2d");
        const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
        const pad = opts.pad ?? 12;
        let W = 0, H = 0, k = 1, ox = 0, oy = 0, paths = [], boxes = [];
        const lonC = Math.cos(((B.n + B.s) / 2) * Math.PI / 180);
        function project() {
          const host = canvas.parentElement;
          W = host.clientWidth; H = host.clientHeight;
          if (!W || !H) return false;
          canvas.width = W * dpr; canvas.height = H * dpr;
          canvas.style.width = W + "px"; canvas.style.height = H + "px";
          ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
          hitCtx.canvas.width = W; hitCtx.canvas.height = H;
          k = Math.min((W - 2 * pad) / ((B.e - B.w) * lonC), (H - 2 * pad) / (B.n - B.s));
          ox = (W - k * (B.e - B.w) * lonC) / 2; oy = (H + k * (B.n - B.s)) / 2;
          paths = []; boxes = [];
          for (const f of geo.features) {
            const p = new Path2D();
            let x0 = Infinity, y0 = Infinity, x1 = -Infinity, y1 = -Infinity;
            const polys = f.geometry.type === "Polygon" ? [f.geometry.coordinates] : f.geometry.coordinates;
            for (const poly of polys) for (const ring of poly) {
              ring.forEach(([lon, lat], j) => {
                const px = X(lon), py = Y(lat);
                if (px < x0) x0 = px; if (px > x1) x1 = px;
                if (py < y0) y0 = py; if (py > y1) y1 = py;
                j ? p.lineTo(px, py) : p.moveTo(px, py);
              });
              p.closePath();
            }
            paths.push(p); boxes.push([x0, y0, x1, y1]);
          }
          return true;
        }
        function X(lon) { return ox + (lon - B.w) * lonC * k; }
        function Y(lat) { return oy - (lat - B.s) * k; }
        function featureAt(ev) {
          const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
          const px = ev.clientX - r.left, py = ev.clientY - r.top;
          for (let i = paths.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            const b = boxes[i];
            if (px < b[0] || px > b[2] || py < b[1] || py > b[3]) continue;
            if (hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py)) return i;
          }
          return -1;
        }
        return { ctx, X, Y, project, featureAt, get paths() { return paths; },
                 get W() { return W; }, get H() { return H; },
                 get pxPerKm() { return k / 110.57; }, canvas };
      }

      function drawNetwork(m, { alpha = 1, modes = null, glow = true, reachedUntil = null } = {}) {
        const { ctx } = m;
        for (const ln of net.lines) {
          if (modes && !modes.has(ln.m)) continue;
          if (!ln.c || ln.c.length < 2) continue;
          const col = MODE_COLOR[ln.m] || "#888";
          const rail = ln.m !== "brt" && ln.m !== "mikrotrans";
          let a = alpha * (ln.m === "mikrotrans" ? 0.5 : rail ? 1 : 0.85);
          if (reachedUntil !== null) {
            const d = ln.__reach ?? 999;
            a *= d <= reachedUntil ? 1 : 0.12;
          }
          ctx.globalAlpha = a;
          ctx.beginPath();
          ln.c.forEach(([lon, lat], i) => (i ? ctx.lineTo(m.X(lon), m.Y(lat)) : ctx.moveTo(m.X(lon), m.Y(lat))));
          if (glow && rail) { ctx.strokeStyle = col; ctx.lineWidth = 5; ctx.globalAlpha = a * 0.16; ctx.stroke(); ctx.globalAlpha = a; }
          ctx.strokeStyle = col;
          ctx.lineWidth = rail ? 1.7 : ln.m === "brt" ? 1.3 : 0.6;
          ctx.lineJoin = "round"; ctx.lineCap = "round";
          ctx.stroke();
        }
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      }

      function drawOutlines(m, { fill = "#14171D", stroke = "#242A34", lw = 0.35, fillFn = null } = {}) {
        const { ctx } = m;
        m.paths.forEach((p, i) => {
          ctx.fillStyle = fillFn ? fillFn(i) : fill;
          ctx.fill(p);
          ctx.strokeStyle = stroke; ctx.lineWidth = lw; ctx.stroke(p);
        });
      }
      /* the base map is not one flat grey: each kelurahan carries a whisper of its own access */
      const baseTint = d3.piecewise(d3.interpolateRgb, ["#0F1218", "#1A1A20", "#2A1D1D", "#3A231B"]);
      const baseFill = geo.features.map((f) => baseTint(shadeT(val(f.properties.id, "all", 60))));

      /* ═════════ HERO — the hour blooming outward ═════════ */
      sect("hero", () => {
        const canvas = document.getElementById("hero-c");
        const m = canvasMap(canvas, { pad: 8 });
        if (!hero || !hero.origins || !Object.keys(hero.origins).length) {
          document.getElementById("hero-stamp").textContent = "Isochrone data pending — the pipeline has not exported hero.json yet.";
          if (m.project()) { drawOutlines(m); drawNetwork(m, { alpha: 0.8 }); }
          return;
        }
        const ids = hero.featured.filter((i) => hero.origins[i]);
        let cur = ids.indexOf(hero.default); if (cur < 0) cur = 0;

        // pre-compute, per line, the earliest minute at which any of its vertices is reached
        const cellLat = cells.lat, cellLon = cells.lon;
        function annotateLines(iso) {
          const tByCell = new Map();
          iso.i.forEach((ci, j) => tByCell.set(ci, iso.t[j]));
          const near = [];
          for (const [ci, t] of tByCell) near.push([cellLon[ci], cellLat[ci], t]);
          for (const ln of net.lines) {
            let best = 999;
            for (let j = 0; j < ln.c.length; j += Math.max(1, Math.floor(ln.c.length / 24))) {
              const [lo, la] = ln.c[j];
              for (const [x, y, t] of near) {
                if (t >= best) continue;
                if (Math.abs(x - lo) < 0.012 && Math.abs(y - la) < 0.012) best = t;
              }
            }
            ln.__reach = best;
          }
        }

        const hud = document.getElementById("hero-hud");
        const clock = document.getElementById("hud-clock");
        const cellPx = () => Math.max(2.2, m.pxPerKm * (cells.cell_m / 1000) * 1.08);
        let raf = null;

        function run(id, animate = true) {
          const iso = hero.origins[id];
          if (!iso) return;
          annotateLines(iso);
          const r = rows[id] || {};
          document.getElementById("hud-origin").textContent = `${r.n ?? id}, ${r.r ?? ""}`.replace(/, $/, "");
          const a60 = r.all ? r.all["60"] : null;
          document.getElementById("hud-jobs").textContent = a60 ? pct(a60[0]) : "—";
          document.getElementById("hud-hosp").textContent = a60 ? num(a60[1]) : "—";
          document.getElementById("hud-pop").textContent = a60 ? pct(a60[2]) : "—";
          hud.hidden = false;
          const px = cellPx();
          const oLat = r.lat, oLon = r.lon;
          const start = performance.now();
          const DUR = 4200;
          cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
          const frame = (now) => {
            const t = reduced ? 60 : Math.min(60, ((now - start) / DUR) * 60);
            clock.textContent = `${String(Math.floor(t)).padStart(2, "0")}:${String(Math.floor((t % 1) * 60)).padStart(2, "0")}`;
            const { ctx } = m;
            ctx.clearRect(0, 0, m.W, m.H);
            ctx.fillStyle = "#0B0D11"; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, m.W, m.H);
            drawOutlines(m, { fillFn: (i) => baseFill[i], stroke: "#1D222B", lw: 0.3 });
            // reachable cells, igniting by band
            ctx.globalCompositeOperation = "lighter";
            for (let j = 0; j < iso.i.length; j++) {
              const tt = iso.t[j]; if (tt > t) break;
              const age = Math.min(1, (t - tt) / 6);
              const ci = iso.i[j];
              const x = m.X(cellLon[ci]), y = m.Y(cellLat[ci]);
              ctx.fillStyle = BAND[bandOf(tt)];
              const halo = px * (1.5 + 0.7 * age);             // soft spill, additively blended
              ctx.globalAlpha = 0.1 + 0.13 * age;
              ctx.fillRect(x - halo / 2, y - halo / 2, halo, halo);
              const core = px * (0.5 + 0.5 * age);             // the cell itself
              ctx.globalAlpha = 0.3 + 0.55 * age;
              ctx.fillRect(x - core / 2, y - core / 2, core, core);
            }
            ctx.globalCompositeOperation = "source-over";
            ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
            drawNetwork(m, { alpha: 0.95, reachedUntil: t });
            // the origin, pulsing
            if (isFinite(oLat) && isFinite(oLon)) {
              const x = m.X(oLon), y = m.Y(oLat);
              const pulse = 6 + (reduced ? 0 : 3 * Math.sin(now / 300));
              const g = ctx.createRadialGradient(x, y, 0, x, y, pulse * 3);
              g.addColorStop(0, "rgba(247,156,106,0.9)"); g.addColorStop(1, "rgba(247,156,106,0)");
              ctx.fillStyle = g; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, pulse * 3, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
              ctx.fillStyle = "#FFF3E9"; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 2.6, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
            }
            const heroVisible = document.getElementById("hero").getBoundingClientRect().bottom > 0;
            if (t < 60 || (!reduced && heroVisible)) raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
          };
          if (!animate || reduced) { clock.textContent = "60:00"; }
          raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
        }
        const boot = () => { if (m.project()) run(ids[cur]); };
        boot();
        addEventListener("resize", () => { if (m.project()) run(ids[cur], false); });
        document.getElementById("hero-replay").onclick = () => run(ids[cur]);
        document.getElementById("hero-shuffle").onclick = () => { cur = (cur + 1) % ids.length; run(ids[cur]); };
      });

      /* ═════════ CH 1 — the assembled network ═════════ */
      sect("network chapter", () => {
        const canvas = document.getElementById("net-c");
        const m = canvasMap(canvas, { pad: 10 });
        const active = new Set(Object.keys(MODE_COLOR));
        const counts = {}; const kms = {};
        const R = 6371;
        for (const ln of net.lines) {
          counts[ln.m] = (counts[ln.m] || 0) + 1;
          let d = 0;
          for (let i = 1; i < ln.c.length; i++) {
            const [x1, y1] = ln.c[i - 1], [x2, y2] = ln.c[i];
            const dx = (x2 - x1) * Math.cos(y1 * Math.PI / 180) * 111.32, dy = (y2 - y1) * 110.57;
            d += Math.hypot(dx, dy);
          }
          kms[ln.m] = (kms[ln.m] || 0) + d;
        }
        const legend = document.getElementById("net-legend");
        legend.innerHTML = "";
        for (const k of Object.keys(MODE_COLOR)) {
          if (!counts[k]) continue;
          const b = document.createElement("button");
          b.type = "button"; b.className = "lg on"; b.dataset.mode = k;
          b.innerHTML = `<i style="background:${MODE_COLOR[k]}"></i><span>${MODE_LABEL[k]}</span><em>${counts[k]} route${counts[k] > 1 ? "s" : ""} · ${Math.round(kms[k])} km</em>`;
          b.onclick = () => { active.has(k) ? active.delete(k) : active.add(k); b.classList.toggle("on"); paint(); };
          legend.appendChild(b);
        }
        const g = stats?.gtfs ?? {};
        const tj = g["transjakarta.zip"] ?? {};
        const rail = g["rail_handencoded.zip"] ?? {};
        const cards = [
          ["Bus routes in the official feed", num(tj.routes)],
          ["Bus stops", num(tj.stops)],
          ["Rail stations (hand-encoded)", num(rail.stops)],
          ["Kelurahan / desa routed", num(access.order.length)],
          ["Destination cells (1 km)", num(cells.lat.length)],
          ["Departure window", `${access.window.from}–${access.window.to}`],
        ];
        document.getElementById("net-stats").innerHTML = cards
          .map(([l, v]) => `<div class="stat"><span class="sv">${v}</span><span class="sl">${l}</span></div>`).join("");
        function paint() {
          if (!m.project()) return;
          const { ctx } = m;
          ctx.fillStyle = "#0C0F13"; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, m.W, m.H);
          drawOutlines(m, { fillFn: (i) => baseFill[i], stroke: "#1E232C", lw: 0.3 });
          drawNetwork(m, { modes: active, alpha: 1 });
          labelLineEnds();
        }
        /* rail line names at the line ends, with bounding-box de-collision */
        function labelLineEnds() {
          const { ctx } = m;
          ctx.font = "600 12px " + getComputedStyle(document.body).getPropertyValue("--font-data");
          ctx.textBaseline = "middle";
          const placed = [];
          const fits = (b) => !placed.some((q) => !(b[2] < q[0] || b[0] > q[2] || b[3] < q[1] || b[1] > q[3]))
            && b[0] > 2 && b[2] < m.W - 2 && b[1] > 2 && b[3] < m.H - 2;
          for (const ln of net.lines) {
            if (ln.m === "brt" || ln.m === "mikrotrans" || !active.has(ln.m) || !ln.c?.length) continue;
            const label = (ln.n || "").replace(/Krl |Lrt |Mrt /i, (x) => x.toUpperCase());
            const w = ctx.measureText(label).width;
            const cx = m.W / 2, cy = m.H / 2;
            const ends = [ln.c[ln.c.length - 1], ln.c[0]].sort((a, b) =>
              Math.hypot(m.X(b[0]) - cx, m.Y(b[1]) - cy) - Math.hypot(m.X(a[0]) - cx, m.Y(a[1]) - cy));
            for (const [lon, lat] of ends) {
              const x = m.X(lon), y = m.Y(lat);
              let done = false;
              for (const [dx, dy] of [[9, 0], [-9 - w, 0], [9, -13], [-9 - w, 13]]) {
                const b = [x + dx - 3, y + dy - 8, x + dx + w + 3, y + dy + 8];
                if (!fits(b)) continue;
                ctx.fillStyle = "rgba(12,15,19,0.78)";
                ctx.fillRect(b[0], b[1], b[2] - b[0], b[3] - b[1]);
                ctx.fillStyle = MODE_COLOR[ln.m];
                ctx.fillText(label, x + dx, y + dy);
                ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 2.2, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
                placed.push(b); done = true; break;
              }
              if (done) break;
            }
          }
        }
        paint();
        addEventListener("resize", paint);
      });

      /* ═════════ CH 2 — choropleth (MapLibre where WebGL exists, canvas otherwise) ═════════ */
      let isochrones = null, isoPending = false;
      const tip = document.getElementById("tip");
      const panel = document.getElementById("panel");

      sect("controls", () => {
        const cut = document.getElementById("cutoff");
        access.cutoffs.forEach((c) => {
          const b = document.createElement("button");
          b.type = "button"; b.textContent = `${c} min`; b.className = c === state.cutoff ? "on" : "";
          b.onclick = () => { state.cutoff = c; [...cut.children].forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b)); repaint(); };
          cut.appendChild(b);
        });
        const sc = document.getElementById("scenario");
        const LAB = { all: "Everything", no_rail: "Without rail", walk: "Walking only" };
        access.scenarios.forEach((s) => {
          const b = document.createElement("button");
          b.type = "button"; b.textContent = LAB[s] ?? s; b.className = s === state.scenario ? "on" : "";
          b.onclick = () => { state.scenario = s; [...sc.children].forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b)); repaint(); };
          sc.appendChild(b);
        });
        const dl = document.getElementById("kel-list");
        for (const id of access.order) {
          const r = rows[id]; if (!r) continue;
          const o = document.createElement("option"); o.value = `${r.n} · ${r.k}, ${r.r}`; o.dataset.id = id; dl.appendChild(o);
        }
        document.getElementById("search").addEventListener("change", (e) => {
          const opt = [...dl.options].find((o) => o.value === e.target.value);
          if (opt) select(opt.dataset.id);
        });
        const rampEl = document.getElementById("ramp");
        rampEl.innerHTML = `<span class="rlab">0%</span><i></i><span class="rlab" id="ramp-max">${pct(maxVal, 0)}</span>
          <span class="rcap">share of the region's job-dense floorspace reachable · square-root scale ·
          mid-tone ≈ ${pct(maxVal * 0.25, 1)} · Kepulauan Seribu is off-frame</span>`;
        rampEl.querySelector("i").style.background = `linear-gradient(90deg, ${RAMP.join(",")})`;
      });

      function tipHTML(id) {
        const r = rows[id]; if (!r) return "";
        const a = r[state.scenario]?.[String(state.cutoff)];
        return `<b>${r.n}</b><span class="t-sub">${r.k} · ${r.r}</span>
          <span class="t-row"><span>Jobs reachable</span><b>${a ? pct(a[0]) : "—"}</b></span>
          <span class="t-row"><span>Hospitals</span><b>${a ? num(a[1]) : "—"}</b></span>
          <span class="t-row"><span>People reachable</span><b>${a ? pct(a[2]) : "—"}</b></span>
          <span class="t-row"><span>Population</span><b>${num(r.pop)}</b></span>
          <span class="t-foot">${state.cutoff} min · scheduled, ${access.window.from}–${access.window.to} weekday</span>`;
      }

      async function loadIsochrones() {
        if (isochrones || isoPending) return isochrones;
        isoPending = true;
        try { isochrones = await fetch(`${base}/data/isochrones.json`).then((r) => r.json()); }
        catch (e) { console.warn("isochrones unavailable", e); }
        isoPending = false; return isochrones;
      }

      async function select(id) {
        state.sel = id;
        tip.hidden = true;
        const r = rows[id]; if (!r) return;
        panel.hidden = false;
        document.getElementById("p-region").textContent = `${r.k} · ${r.r}`;
        document.getElementById("p-name").textContent = r.n;
        const a = r[state.scenario]?.[String(state.cutoff)] ?? [null, null, null, null];
        const x = r[`${state.scenario}_x`] ?? {};
        document.getElementById("p-stats").innerHTML = [
          ["Job-dense floorspace", pct(a[0])],
          ["Hospitals", num(a[1])],
          ["Clinics · puskesmas", num(a[3])],
          ["People reachable", pct(a[2])],
          ["Nearest hospital", x.nh == null ? "—" : `${Math.round(x.nh)} min`],
          ["Population", num(r.pop)],
        ].map(([l, v]) => `<div class="ps"><span class="pv">${v}</span><span class="pl">${l}</span></div>`).join("");
        const bars = access.cutoffs.map((c) => {
          const v = r[state.scenario]?.[String(c)]?.[0] ?? 0;
          return `<div class="bar"><span class="bl">${c} min</span><i style="width:${Math.min(100, (v / maxVal) * 100)}%"></i><b>${pct(v)}</b></div>`;
        }).join("");
        document.getElementById("p-bars").innerHTML = bars;
        const note = document.getElementById("p-note");
        repaint();
        if (!isochrones) note.textContent = "Loading this kelurahan's isochrone…";
        const iso = await loadIsochrones();
        note.textContent = `Scheduled p50 over ${access.window.from}–${access.window.to} on ${access.window.date}. Rail legs carry a ±15 % caveat (hand-encoded timetables).`;
        if (iso && iso[id]) repaint();
        syncHash();
      }
      document.getElementById("panel-close").onclick = () => { panel.hidden = true; state.sel = null; repaint(); syncHash(); };
      const syncHash = () => { history.replaceState(null, "", state.sel ? `#k=${state.sel}` : " "); };

      let repaint = () => {};
      sect("choropleth", () => {
        const host = document.getElementById("map");
        let webgl = false;
        try {
          const c = document.createElement("canvas");
          webgl = !!(c.getContext("webgl2") || c.getContext("webgl"));
        } catch (e) { webgl = false; }
        if (webgl) { try { return webglMap(); } catch (e) { console.warn("WebGL map failed, using canvas:", e); } }
        return canvasChoropleth();

        function shadeGeo() {
          for (const f of geo.features) {
            const v = val(f.properties.id);
            f.properties.v = shadeT(v);
          }
        }

        function webglMap() {
          shadeGeo();
          const map = new maplibregl.Map({
            container: "map", attributionControl: false, dragRotate: false,
            style: { version: 8, sources: {}, layers: [{ id: "bg", type: "background", paint: { "background-color": "#0C0F13" } }] },
            bounds: [[B.w, B.s], [B.e, B.n]], fitBoundsOptions: { padding: 18 },
          });
          map.addControl(new maplibregl.AttributionControl({ customAttribution: "COD-AB (BPS) · OSM ODbL · GHSL", compact: true }));
          map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl({ showCompass: false }));
          map.on("load", () => {
            map.addSource("adm4", { type: "geojson", data: geo, promoteId: "id" });
            map.addLayer({ id: "fill", type: "fill", source: "adm4",
              paint: { "fill-color": ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["get", "v"], 0, RAMP[0], 0.2, RAMP[1], 0.4, RAMP[2], 0.6, RAMP[3], 0.8, RAMP[4], 1, RAMP[5]], "fill-opacity": 0.94 } });
            map.addLayer({ id: "line", type: "line", source: "adm4", paint: { "line-color": "#20252E", "line-width": 0.3 } });
            map.addLayer({ id: "sel", type: "line", source: "adm4", paint: { "line-color": "#F79C6A", "line-width": 1.8 }, filter: ["==", ["get", "id"], ""] });
            const lineFC = { type: "FeatureCollection", features: net.lines.map((l) => ({ type: "Feature", properties: { m: l.m }, geometry: { type: "LineString", coordinates: l.c } })) };
            map.addSource("net", { type: "geojson", data: lineFC });
            map.addSource("iso", { type: "geojson", data: { type: "FeatureCollection", features: [] } });
            map.addLayer({ id: "iso", type: "circle", source: "iso",
              paint: { "circle-radius": ["interpolate", ["exponential", 2], ["zoom"], 8, 2.5, 12, 26],
                       "circle-color": ["step", ["get", "t"], BAND[0], 15, BAND[1], 30, BAND[2], 45, BAND[3]],
                       "circle-opacity": 0.5, "circle-blur": 0.35 } });
            map.addLayer({ id: "net", type: "line", source: "net",
              paint: { "line-color": ["match", ["get", "m"], "brt", MODE_COLOR.brt, "mikrotrans", MODE_COLOR.mikrotrans, "krl", MODE_COLOR.krl, "mrt", MODE_COLOR.mrt, "lrt", MODE_COLOR.lrt, "#888"],
                       "line-width": 0.9, "line-opacity": 0.5 } });
          });
          map.on("mousemove", "fill", (e) => {
            const f = e.features[0];
            map.setFilter("sel", ["==", ["get", "id"], f.properties.id]);
            map.getCanvas().style.cursor = "pointer";
            tip.hidden = false; tip.style.left = e.point.x + 16 + "px"; tip.style.top = e.point.y + 16 + "px";
            tip.innerHTML = tipHTML(f.properties.id);
          });
          map.on("mouseleave", "fill", () => { map.setFilter("sel", ["==", ["get", "id"], ""]); tip.hidden = true; map.getCanvas().style.cursor = ""; });
          map.on("click", "fill", (e) => select(e.features[0].properties.id));
          repaint = () => {
            shadeGeo();
            map.getSource("adm4")?.setData(geo);
            map.setFilter?.("sel", ["==", ["get", "id"], state.sel ?? ""]);
            const iso = isochrones?.[state.sel]?.[state.scenario] ?? (state.scenario === "all" && state.sel ? hero?.origins?.[state.sel] : null);
            const feats = [];
            if (iso) for (let j = 0; j < iso.i.length; j++) {
              const tt = iso.t[j]; if (tt > state.cutoff) break;
              feats.push({ type: "Feature", properties: { t: tt },
                geometry: { type: "Point", coordinates: [cells.lon[iso.i[j]], cells.lat[iso.i[j]]] } });
            }
            map.getSource("iso")?.setData({ type: "FeatureCollection", features: feats });
          };
          return map;
        }

        function canvasChoropleth() {
          host.innerHTML = "";
          const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
          canvas.style.cssText = "display:block;cursor:crosshair;";
          host.appendChild(canvas);
          const note = document.createElement("div");
          note.className = "map-note";
          note.textContent = "2-D CANVAS MAP (BROWSER GPU OFF) · FULLY INTERACTIVE";
          host.appendChild(note);
          const m = canvasMap(canvas, { pad: 14 });
          let hover = -1;
          const cellPx = () => Math.max(2.4, m.pxPerKm * (cells.cell_m / 1000) * 1.04);
          function paint() {
            if (!m.project()) return;
            const { ctx } = m;
            ctx.fillStyle = "#0C0F13"; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, m.W, m.H);
            geo.features.forEach((f, i) => {
              const v = val(f.properties.id);
              ctx.fillStyle = v == null ? "#12151B" : ramp(shadeT(v));
              ctx.fill(m.paths[i]);
              ctx.strokeStyle = "#1B2029"; ctx.lineWidth = 0.3; ctx.stroke(m.paths[i]);
            });
            drawNetwork(m, { alpha: 0.45, glow: false });
            const iso = isochrones?.[state.sel]?.[state.scenario] ?? (state.scenario === "all" && state.sel ? hero?.origins?.[state.sel] : null);
            if (iso) {
              const px = cellPx();
              ctx.globalCompositeOperation = "lighter";
              for (let j = 0; j < iso.i.length; j++) {
                const t = iso.t[j]; if (t > state.cutoff) break;
                const x = m.X(cells.lon[iso.i[j]]), y = m.Y(cells.lat[iso.i[j]]);
                ctx.fillStyle = BAND[bandOf(t)];
                ctx.globalAlpha = 0.16;
                ctx.fillRect(x - px, y - px, px * 2, px * 2);
                ctx.globalAlpha = 0.62;
                ctx.fillRect(x - px / 2, y - px / 2, px, px);
              }
              ctx.globalCompositeOperation = "source-over"; ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
              const r = rows[state.sel];
              if (r && isFinite(r.lat)) {                       // where the hour starts
                const x = m.X(r.lon), y = m.Y(r.lat);
                ctx.strokeStyle = "#FFF3E9"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
                ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 7, 0, 7); ctx.stroke();
                ctx.fillStyle = "#FFF3E9";
                ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 2.6, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
              }
            }
            const selIdx = state.sel ? geo.features.findIndex((f) => f.properties.id === state.sel) : -1;
            if (selIdx >= 0) { ctx.strokeStyle = "#F79C6A"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.8; ctx.stroke(m.paths[selIdx]); }
            if (hover >= 0) { ctx.strokeStyle = "#FFF3E9"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.2; ctx.stroke(m.paths[hover]); }
          }
          canvas.addEventListener("mousemove", (e) => {
            const i = m.featureAt(e);
            if (i !== hover) { hover = i; paint(); }
            if (i < 0) { tip.hidden = true; return; }
            const r = host.getBoundingClientRect();
            const blocked = panel && !panel.hidden && getComputedStyle(panel).position === "absolute"
              ? panel.offsetWidth + 28 : 0;
            tip.hidden = false;
            tip.style.left = Math.max(8, Math.min(e.clientX - r.left + 16,
              host.clientWidth - 250 - blocked)) + "px";
            tip.style.top = Math.min(e.clientY - r.top + 16, host.clientHeight - 160) + "px";
            tip.innerHTML = tipHTML(geo.features[i].properties.id);
          });
          const hideTip = () => { if (!tip.hidden || hover >= 0) { hover = -1; tip.hidden = true; paint(); } };
          canvas.addEventListener("mouseleave", hideTip);
          /* mouseleave is the happy path, but a pointer can stop hovering without ever
             firing one: the window loses focus (an app switch, a screenshot), the tab is
             hidden, or the pointer is already elsewhere when something repaints. Any of
             those stranded the read-out on screen. Treat "a pointer moving anywhere that
             is not this canvas" as the authoritative signal that hovering has ended. */
          canvas.addEventListener("pointerleave", hideTip);
          document.addEventListener("pointermove", (e) => { if (e.target !== canvas) hideTip(); }, { passive: true });
          document.addEventListener("pointerdown", (e) => { if (e.target !== canvas) hideTip(); }, { passive: true });
          addEventListener("blur", hideTip);
          document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", () => { if (document.hidden) hideTip(); });
          canvas.addEventListener("click", (e) => { const i = m.featureAt(e); if (i >= 0) select(geo.features[i].properties.id); });
          canvas.tabIndex = 0;
          repaint = paint;
          paint();
          addEventListener("resize", paint);
          return { paint };
        }
      });

      /* callouts + so-whats driven by the data, never hard-coded */
      sect("narrative", () => {
        const sAll = equity.scenarios?.all ?? {};
        const pair = equity.pairing ?? {};
        const co = document.getElementById("callouts");
        const items = [];
        const hosp = (v) => (typeof v === "number" ? `${Math.round(v)} min to a hospital` : "no hospital within an hour");
        if (pair.menteng) items.push(["Menteng, Central Jakarta", pct(pair.menteng.pop_weighted_jobs_share, 2), hosp(pair.menteng.median_nearest_hospital_min)]);
        if (pair.bekasi) items.push(["Bekasi", pct(pair.bekasi.pop_weighted_jobs_share, 2), hosp(pair.bekasi.median_nearest_hospital_min)]);
        items.push(["DKI Jakarta, median resident", pct(sAll.dki_median, 2), "population-weighted"]);
        items.push(["Bodetabek, median resident", pct(sAll.bodetabek_median, 2), "population-weighted"]);
        co.innerHTML = items.map(([l, v, s]) => `<div class="callout"><span class="co-v">${v}</span><span class="co-l">${l}</span><span class="co-s">${s}</span></div>`).join("");
        const ratio = sAll.bodetabek_median > 0 ? (sAll.dki_median / sAll.bodetabek_median) : null;
        const c30 = (equity.by_cutoff ?? []).find((r) => r.cutoff === 30);
        document.getElementById("ch2-sowhat").textContent =
          `So what: the median resident of DKI Jakarta reaches ${pct(sAll.dki_median, 2)} of the region's job-dense floorspace in an hour; the median resident of Bodetabek reaches ${pct(sAll.bodetabek_median, 2)}` +
          (ratio && isFinite(ratio) ? ` — a gap of ${ratio.toFixed(0)}× at this cutoff, ${c30 ? `and ${c30.ratio.toFixed(0)}× at thirty minutes. ` : ". "}` : ". ") +
          "Both are gaps in the scheduled network this models; the motorcycles most of the region actually travels on are not routed here.";
        document.getElementById("foot-stamp").textContent =
          `A DEMO-LAB CASE · STATIC SNAPSHOT · ROUTED ${access.window.date} ${access.window.from}–${access.window.to} · GENERATED ${(stats?.generated ?? "").slice(0, 10)}`;
      });

      /* ═════════ CH 3 — Lorenz ═════════ */
      sect("lorenz", () => {
        const sAll = equity.scenarios?.all;
        if (!sAll) return;
        document.getElementById("gini").textContent = fx(sAll.gini);
        document.getElementById("palma").textContent = typeof sAll.palma === "number" ? fx(sAll.palma, 1) + "×" : "∞";
        if (typeof sAll.palma !== "number" && sAll.palma_note)
          document.querySelector("#palma").nextElementSibling.textContent =
            "Palma ratio — undefined here: the bottom four tenths of the population reach essentially nothing";
        document.getElementById("nohosp").textContent = pct(sAll.pop_share_no_hospital_60min, 0);
        const el = document.getElementById("lorenz");
        const W = Math.max(320, (el.clientWidth || 560) - 18), H = Math.min(420, Math.max(300, W * 0.72));
        const M = { t: 18, r: 18, b: 44, l: 52 };
        const x = d3.scaleLinear([0, 1], [M.l, W - M.r]), y = d3.scaleLinear([0, 1], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H).attr("role", "img")
          .attr("aria-label", `Lorenz curve of transit access; Gini ${fx(sAll.gini)}`);
        const defs = svg.append("defs");
        const grad = defs.append("linearGradient").attr("id", "lz").attr("x1", 0).attr("y1", 1).attr("x2", 0).attr("y2", 0);
        grad.append("stop").attr("offset", "0%").attr("stop-color", "#E4562E").attr("stop-opacity", 0.02);
        grad.append("stop").attr("offset", "100%").attr("stop-color", "#E4562E").attr("stop-opacity", 0.34);
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(5).tickFormat(d3.format(".0%")));
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`)
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(5).tickFormat(d3.format(".0%")));
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "axlab").attr("x", (W + M.l) / 2).attr("y", H - 8)
          .attr("text-anchor", "middle").text("cumulative share of people, worst-served first");
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "axlab").attr("transform", `translate(14,${(H - M.b + M.t) / 2}) rotate(-90)`)
          .attr("text-anchor", "middle").text("cumulative share of reachable jobs");
        svg.append("line").attr("x1", x(0)).attr("y1", y(0)).attr("x2", x(1)).attr("y2", y(1))
          .attr("stroke", "#4A5260").attr("stroke-dasharray", "3 4").attr("stroke-width", 1);
        const line = d3.line().x((d) => x(d[0])).y((d) => y(d[1])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        const area = d3.area().x((d) => x(d[0])).y0((d) => y(d[0])).y1((d) => y(d[1])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        const others = ["no_rail", "walk"].filter((s) => equity.scenarios[s]);
        others.forEach((s) => {
          svg.append("path").datum(equity.scenarios[s].lorenz).attr("d", line)
            .attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", s === "walk" ? "#5A6270" : "#8C6A5D")
            .attr("stroke-width", 1.2).attr("stroke-dasharray", "4 4").attr("opacity", 0.9)
            .append("title").text(`${s === "walk" ? "Walking only" : "Without rail"} · Gini ${fx(equity.scenarios[s].gini)}`);
        });
        const fill = svg.append("path").datum(sAll.lorenz).attr("d", area).attr("fill", "url(#lz)").attr("opacity", 0);
        const path = svg.append("path").datum(sAll.lorenz).attr("d", line).attr("fill", "none")
          .attr("stroke", "#E4562E").attr("stroke-width", 2.4).attr("stroke-linecap", "round");
        const len = path.node().getTotalLength();
        const focus = svg.append("g").attr("opacity", 0);
        focus.append("circle").attr("r", 4.5).attr("fill", "#F79C6A");
        const ft = focus.append("text").attr("class", "focus-t").attr("x", 10).attr("y", -10);
        const draw = () => {
          if (reduced) { fill.attr("opacity", 1); return; }
          path.attr("stroke-dasharray", `${len} ${len}`).attr("stroke-dashoffset", len)
            .transition().duration(1400).ease(d3.easeCubicOut).attr("stroke-dashoffset", 0);
          fill.transition().delay(700).duration(700).attr("opacity", 1);
        };
        new IntersectionObserver((es, o) => es.forEach((e) => { if (e.isIntersecting) { draw(); o.disconnect(); } }), { threshold: 0.35 }).observe(el);
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b)
          .attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (ev) => {
            const px = d3.pointer(ev)[0], xv = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, x.invert(px)));
            const c = sAll.lorenz;
            const i = Math.min(c.length - 1, Math.max(0, Math.round(xv * (c.length - 1))));
            focus.attr("opacity", 1).attr("transform", `translate(${x(c[i][0])},${y(c[i][1])})`);
            ft.text(`${d3.format(".0%")(c[i][0])} of people → ${d3.format(".1%")(c[i][1])} of reachable jobs`);
            ft.attr("x", c[i][0] > 0.5 ? -10 : 10).attr("text-anchor", c[i][0] > 0.5 ? "end" : "start");
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => focus.attr("opacity", 0));

        const tbl = (arr, el2) => {
          document.getElementById(el2).innerHTML = `<table><thead><tr><th>Kelurahan</th><th>Kabupaten / kota</th><th class="r">Jobs in 60 min</th><th class="r">Hospitals</th></tr></thead><tbody>` +
            arr.map((r) => `<tr><td>${r.adm4_name}</td><td class="dim">${r.adm2_name}</td><td class="r num">${pct(r.jobs_share)}</td><td class="r num">${num(r.hospitals)}</td></tr>`).join("") +
            `</tbody></table>`;
        };
        tbl(equity.best ?? [], "tbl-best");
        tbl(equity.worst ?? [], "tbl-worst");
        /* the hour is a choice — publish what the other choices give */
        const bc = equity.by_cutoff ?? [];
        if (bc.length) {
          document.getElementById("cutstrip").innerHTML =
            `<div class="cs-h"><span>If the hour were shorter</span></div>` +
            `<table><thead><tr><th>Time budget</th><th class="r">Gini</th><th class="r">Palma</th><th class="r">DKI</th><th class="r">Bodetabek</th><th class="r">Gap</th></tr></thead><tbody>` +
            bc.map((r) => `<tr class="${r.cutoff === 60 ? "on" : ""}"><td>${r.cutoff} minutes${r.cutoff === 60 ? " · published" : ""}</td>` +
              `<td class="r num">${fx(r.gini)}</td><td class="r num">${fx(r.palma, 1)}×</td>` +
              `<td class="r num">${pct(r.dki_median, 2)}</td><td class="r num">${pct(r.bodetabek_median, 2)}</td>` +
              `<td class="r num">${r.ratio ? r.ratio.toFixed(0) + "×" : "—"}</td></tr>`).join("") +
            `</tbody></table>`;
        }
        const c30 = bc.find((r) => r.cutoff === 30);
        const pl = equity.poverty_link ?? {};
        document.getElementById("ch3-sowhat").textContent =
          `So what: a Gini of ${fx(sAll.gini)} on access is not an income Gini and should not be read as one — a hard 60-minute cut-off manufactures exact zeros that an income distribution never has, and it is a property of the chosen hour as much as of the network` +
          (c30 ? `: cut the budget to 30 minutes and the same data gives ${fx(c30.gini)}, with a Palma of ${fx(c30.palma, 1)}× instead of ${fx(sAll.palma, 1)}×. ` : ". ") +
          (pl.available ? `Against Case F's kecamatan poverty estimates the rank correlation is ${pl.spearman_rho.toFixed(2)} and the concentration index is ${fx(pl.concentration_index)} — access accrues to the less poor. In the poorest fifth of kelurahan ${pct(pl.quintiles[pl.quintiles.length - 1].zero_share, 0)} reach no measured job-dense floorspace at all in an hour; in the least-poor fifth, ${pct(pl.quintiles[0].zero_share, 0)}.`
                        : `The poverty cross-link is pending: ${(pl.reason ?? "Case F has not published its estimates yet").replace(/\.$/, "")}.`);
      });

      /* ═════════ CH 4 — what each layer buys ═════════ */
      sect("layers", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("layers");
        const S = equity.scenarios ?? {};
        const order = ["all", "no_rail", "walk"].filter((s) => S[s]);
        const LAB = { all: "Everything: bus + rail + walking", no_rail: "Without rail (bus + walking)", walk: "Walking only" };
        const maxM = Math.max(...order.map((s) => S[s].mean_jobs_share), 0.0001);
        el.innerHTML = order.map((s) => {
          const v = S[s];
          return `<div class="layer">
            <div class="layer-h"><span class="layer-n">${LAB[s]}</span><span class="layer-v">${pct(v.mean_jobs_share, 2)}</span></div>
            <div class="layer-bar"><i data-w="${Math.max(1.5, (v.mean_jobs_share / maxM) * 100)}"></i></div>
            <div class="layer-m"><span>average resident, population-weighted</span><span>median resident <b>${pct(v.median_jobs_share, 2)}</b></span><span>Gini <b>${fx(v.gini)}</b></span><span>DKI <b>${pct(v.dki_median, 2)}</b></span><span>Bodetabek <b>${pct(v.bodetabek_median, 2)}</b></span><span>hospital <b>${typeof v.median_nearest_hospital_min === "number" ? Math.round(v.median_nearest_hospital_min) + " min" : "—"}</b></span></div>
          </div>`;
        }).join("");
        const bars = el.querySelectorAll(".layer-bar i");
        const run = () => bars.forEach((b, i) => setTimeout(() => { b.style.width = b.dataset.w + "%"; }, reduced ? 0 : 120 * i));
        new IntersectionObserver((es, o) => es.forEach((e) => { if (e.isIntersecting) { run(); o.disconnect(); } }), { threshold: 0.3 }).observe(el);
        const rc = equity.rail_contribution, tc = equity.transit_contribution, inc = equity.incidence;
        document.getElementById("ch4-sowhat").textContent =
          (tc ? `So what: the whole public-transport system is worth ${pct(Math.abs(tc.mean_access_delta ?? 0), 2)} of reachable floorspace over walking alone, and the rail layer ${pct(Math.abs(rc?.mean_access_delta ?? 0), 2)} of that. ` : "So what: ") +
          (inc?.transit ? `But a mean says nothing about who: ${pct(inc.transit.dki_share_of_gain, 0)} of what the system adds goes to the ${pct(inc.dki_pop_share, 0)} of the region's people who live inside DKI, and ${pct(inc.rail.dki_share_of_gain, 0)} of what rail adds. ` : "") +
          (typeof tc?.gini_delta === "number" ? `Every layer raises access everywhere and raises the Gini with it — from ${fx(S.walk?.gini)} on foot to ${fx(S.all?.gini)} with everything. In relative terms this network concentrates opportunity; in absolute terms nobody loses. Both are true, and the periphery's angkot are missing from both.` : "");
      });

      /* ═════════ METHOD ═════════ */
      sect("method", () => {
        const g = document.getElementById("gates");
        if (!stats) { g.innerHTML = `<p class="pending">Gate results pending — validate.py has not run for this build.</p>`; }
        else {
          const rowsG = [];
          let checkNo = 0;   // readers get a plain handle, not an internal code
          const mk = (id, title, body, ok) => rowsG.push(`<div class="gate ${ok === true ? "ok" : ok === false ? "bad" : "na"}">
            <span class="g-id">CHECK ${++checkNo}</span><div><b>${title}</b><p>${body}</p></div>
            <span class="g-flag">${ok === true ? "PASS" : ok === false ? "FAIL" : "PENDING"}</span></div>`);
          const g1 = stats["G-G1"] ?? {};
          mk("G-G1", "Timetable sanity", ((g1.ods ?? []).map((o) =>
            (typeof o.scheduled_kmh === "number"
              ? `${o.name}: published corridor average <b>${o.published_kmh} km/h</b>, the operator's own feed schedules <b>${o.scheduled_kmh} km/h</b> across ${num(o.trips_matched)} trips`
              : `${o.name}: operator publishes <b>${o.published_min} min</b>, our timetable schedules <b>${o.scheduled_in_vehicle_min ?? "—"} min</b>`) +
            `${typeof o.router_door_to_door_min === "number" ? ` (router door-to-door, incl. walk + wait: ${Math.round(o.router_door_to_door_min)} min)` : ""}` +
            `${o.note ? ` — ${o.note}` : ""}`).join("<br>") || "not evaluated") +
            (g1.method ? `<br><span class="dim">${g1.method}.</span>` : ""), g1.pass);
          const g2 = stats["G-G2"] ?? {};
          mk("G-G2", "External routing check", g2.reason ?? "not evaluated", null);
          const g3 = stats["G-G3"] ?? {};
          mk("G-G3", "Network integrity",
            `${num(g3.stops)} GTFS stops; ${g3.snap_share == null ? (g3.snap_note ?? "snap test unavailable") : pct(g3.snap_share, 2) + " snap to the street graph within 200 m"}. ` +
            `${num(g3.unreachable_origins)} of ${num(g3.origins)} origins could not be routed at all` +
            `${g3.unreachable_kepulauan_seribu ? ` (${g3.unreachable_kepulauan_seribu} of them Kepulauan Seribu, which has no road link to the mainland and sits outside the routable clip; ${num(g3.unreachable_mainland)} on the mainland)` : ""}. ` +
            `<span class="dim">${g3.note ?? ""}</span>`, g3.pass);
          const g4 = stats["G-G4"] ?? {};
          const pnt = g4.people_near_transit ?? {};
          mk("G-G4", "Plausibility", [
            g4.monotonicity ? `Rail ≥ no-rail everywhere: ${num(g4.monotonicity.violations_material ?? g4.monotonicity.violations)} material violations of ${num(g4.monotonicity.origins)} origins` +
              `${g4.monotonicity.violations_exact != null ? ` (${num(g4.monotonicity.violations_exact)} below the ${pct(g4.monotonicity.tolerance_share, 1)} tolerance — R5 samples frequency headways by Monte Carlo)` : ""}.` : "",
            g4.core_periphery ? `DKI median ${pct(g4.core_periphery.dki_median, 2)} vs Bodetabek ${pct(g4.core_periphery.bodetabek_median, 2)}.` : "",
            pnt.Jakarta ? `People-near-transit (≤15-min headway, 1 km): Jakarta ${pct(pnt.Jakarta.share, 0)} vs ITDP's 2016 anchor 44%; Greater Jakarta ${pct(pnt["Greater Jakarta"].share, 0)} vs 16%.` +
              `${pnt.method ? `<br><span class="dim">${pnt.method}</span>` : ""}` +
              `<br><span class="dim"><b>Read this as coverage, not as a test.</b> ITDP's 2016 figure counts only rapid transit — in Jakarta that year, BRT corridors alone, and its metro row uses the same numerator as its city row because the network did not leave the city. This counts every stop with a headway of 15 minutes or better, Mikrotrans and commuter rail included, so it measures a different thing. At ${pct(pnt.Jakarta.share, 0)} of Jakarta it also has almost no room to discriminate: nearly any network would pass it.</span>` : "",
          ].filter(Boolean).join("<br>"), g4.pass);
          g.innerHTML = rowsG.join("");
        }
        const rail = stats?.rail_handencoded;
        document.getElementById("rail-table").innerHTML = rail
          ? `<p class="dim">${rail.note}</p><table><thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Operator</th><th class="r">Peak headway</th><th class="r">Avg speed</th><th class="r">Stations</th></tr></thead><tbody>` +
            Object.entries(rail.lines).map(([k, v]) => `<tr><td>${k.replace(/_/g, " ")}</td><td class="dim">${v.operator}</td><td class="r num">${v.headway_peak_min} min</td><td class="r num">${v.avg_commercial_kmh} km/h</td><td class="r num">${v.stations}</td></tr>`).join("") +
            `</tbody></table><p class="dim">Headway sources: ${[...new Set(Object.values(rail.lines).map((v) => v.headway_source))].join(" · ")}. Geometry: ${rail.geometry_licence}.</p>`
          : `<p class="pending">Hand-encoded rail table pending.</p>`;
        const inputs = stats?.inputs ?? {};
        const SRC = [
          ["TransJakarta GTFS", "Licence <b>not stated</b> by the operator, Transitland or the Mobility Database — used with attribution while written confirmation is sought.", inputs.gtfs_transjakarta?.last_modified ?? inputs.gtfs_transjakarta?.fetched],
          ["OpenStreetMap (Geofabrik java-latest)", "ODbL 1.0 — street and footpath graph, rail geometry, station names.", inputs.osm_java_pbf?.fetched],
          ["GHSL GHS-BUILT-S NRES E2020", "CC BY 4.0 (JRC) — the jobs proxy: non-residential built-up floorspace.", "2020 epoch"],
          ["GHSL GHS-POP E2025", "CC BY 4.0 (JRC) — population surface.", "2025 epoch"],
          ["HDX healthsites", "ODbL — hospitals, clinics and puskesmas.", inputs.healthsites?.fetched],
          ["HDX COD-AB (BPS)", "CC BY-IGO — the 1,511 kelurahan / desa boundaries.", inputs.codab_adm4?.fetched],
          ["Bogor angkot GTFS", "CC0 community feed (Mobility Database).", inputs.gtfs_bogor?.fetched],
          ["r5py / R5", "MIT / GPL-3.0-or-later — frequency-aware RAPTOR routing.", "1.1.7"],
        ];
        document.getElementById("sources").innerHTML = `<table><tbody>` + SRC.map(([n, l, v]) =>
          `<tr><td><b>${n}</b><br><span class="dim">${l}</span></td><td class="r dim num">${v ?? "—"}</td></tr>`).join("") + `</tbody></table>`;

        /* Limits the review stage measured rather than asserted. Every number here is read
           from data/review_summary.json, so this list cannot drift from the pipeline. */
        const rv = review;
        const cut = equity.by_cutoff ?? [];
        const lim = [];
        if (cut.length >= 2) {
          const lo = cut[0], hi = cut[cut.length - 1];
          lim.push(`<li><b>The hour is a choice, and it changes the answer.</b> A cumulative-opportunity measure counts everything inside a time boundary and nothing outside it. At ${lo.cutoff} minutes the core-to-periphery gap is ${lo.ratio?.toFixed(0)}× and the Gini ${fx(lo.gini)}; at ${hi.cutoff} minutes they are ${hi.ratio?.toFixed(0)}× and ${fx(hi.gini)}. All three budgets are published in chapter 03 rather than one.</li>`);
        }
        if (rv?.volume) {
          lim.push(`<li><b>Floor plan, not floor area.</b> The proxy is built <i>surface</i> (GHS-BUILT-S), so a warehouse counts its footprint and a tower counts its footprint too — the region averages ${fx(rv.volume.mean_storeys, 1)} storeys. Re-measured on the matching building-<i>volume</i> product the DKI median rises from ${pct(rv.volume.dki_median_surface, 1)} to ${pct(rv.volume.dki_median_volume, 1)} and the gap widens from ${rv.volume.ratio_surface?.toFixed(0)}× to ${rv.volume.ratio_volume?.toFixed(0)}×, while the ranking of kelurahan is unchanged (ρ ${fx(rv.volume.rho)}). The levels here understate concentration; the ordering survives.</li>`);
        }
        if (rv?.maup) {
          const L = rv.maup.levels;
          lim.push(`<li><b>Kelurahan are not equal-sized.</b> They run from ${fx(rv.maup.area_min, 2)} km² to ${fx(rv.maup.area_max, 1)} km², a ${num(rv.maup.area_ratio)}-fold range, so one routed point stands for very different amounts of ground. Re-aggregated to ${L[L.length - 1].level} the same data gives a Gini of ${fx(L[L.length - 1].gini)} and a Palma of ${fx(L[L.length - 1].palma, 1)}× instead of ${fx(L[0].gini)} and ${fx(L[0].palma, 1)}×.</li>`);
        }
        if (rv?.rail_optimism) {
          lim.push(`<li><b>The hand-encoded rail runs fast, systematically.</b> All three lines with a published end-to-end time are scheduled ${pct(rv.rail_optimism.min, 1)}–${pct(rv.rail_optimism.max, 1)} quicker than the operator says, in the same direction, because run times are laid along straight lines between stations while the operator's time is for the real, longer alignment: the average chord shortfall is ${pct(rv.rail_optimism.chord_deficit, 1)} against an average optimism of ${pct(rv.rail_optimism.mean, 1)}.</li>`);
        }
        if (rv?.network_failures) {
          lim.push(`<li><b>Some zeros are the network, not the map.</b> ${num(rv.network_failures)} kelurahan — ${num(rv.network_failure_pop)} people — sit within 10 km of more than the median amount of the region's job-dense floorspace and still reach none of it in an hour. That list, not the shading, is what this instrument is for.</li>`);
        }
        if (lim.length) document.getElementById("limits-review").innerHTML = lim.join("");
      });

      /* entrance reveals */
      sect("reveal", () => {
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((es) => es.forEach((e) => { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add("in"); io.unobserve(e.target); } }), { threshold: 0.12 });
        document.querySelectorAll(".reveal").forEach((el) => io.observe(el));
      });

      /* deep link */
      sect("hash", () => {
        const m = location.hash.match(/k=([\w.]+)/);
        if (m && rows[m[1]]) select(m[1]);
      });
    </script>

    <style is:global>
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        margin: 0; background: var(--ground); color: var(--ink);
        font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        background-image: radial-gradient(1200px 600px at 78% -8%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 10%, transparent), transparent 62%);
      }
      h1, h2, h3, h4 { font-family: var(--font-display); margin: 0; text-wrap: balance; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .num, .stamp, .eyebrow, .ch-num, .bignum, .hud-num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
      a { color: var(--accent); }
      :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 3px; }
      button { font: inherit; }

      .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }
      .stamp { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .dim { color: var(--ink-muted); }

      /* ── hero ── */
      .hero { position: relative; min-height: 100svh; display: grid; align-items: end; overflow: hidden; }
      .hero-canvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
      .hero-canvas canvas { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }
      .hero-scrim { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none;
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(11,13,17,0.86) 0%, rgba(11,13,17,0.25) 34%, rgba(11,13,17,0.55) 72%, rgba(11,13,17,0.95) 100%); }
      .hero-copy { position: relative; padding: 0 6vw 8vh; max-width: 60rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
      .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 11vw, 8rem); line-height: 0.9; font-weight: 800;
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, #FFF6F0 10%, #F79C6A 62%, #E4562E 100%);
        -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent; }
      .lede { font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.22rem); color: #CFD3DA; max-width: 46ch; margin: 0; }
      .hero-hud { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 34px; align-items: flex-end; margin-top: 6px;
        border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, transparent); padding-top: 14px; }
      .hud-main { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; }
      .hud-num { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 600; color: #FFD9C4;
        text-shadow: 0 0 26px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, transparent); }
      .hud-lab, .hud-stats span { font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .hud-lab b, .hud-stats b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
      .hud-stats { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
      .hud-actions { display: flex; gap: 8px; }
      .btn { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent); color: #FFD9C4; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 46%, transparent);
